.TH MAKEGHREPO 1
.SH NAME
makeghrepo \- create a configured GitHub repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makeghrepo
[NAME] [LANGUAGE]... [\-\-private] [\-\-lib]
[\-\-license none|MIT] [\-\-no-ci] [\-\-no-pr] [\-\-render DIR]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no-ci
Public repositories only: omit required CI/status checks. Keep required pull
requests and resolved review threads unless --no-pr is also selected. Actions,
workflow files, CodeQL, local bootstrap checks and release CI gates remain.
.TP
.B \-\-no-pr
Public repositories only: omit required pull requests and associated reviews.
CI remains required unless --no-ci is also selected. History protections remain.
.TP
.B \-\-private
Create a private repository. Reject --no-ci and --no-pr. Disable Actions before
publishing, preserving the existing private-repository policy.
.TP
.B \-\-license none|MIT
New projects default to no license. MIT is explicit. Resume preserves licensing;
legacy markers without a license field retain MIT.
.TP
.B \-\-lib
Python library layout; requires the python language.
.TP
.B \-\-render DIR
Render offline into an absent or empty directory, with no checks or GitHub calls.
Supports both policy opt-outs; creates no repository or resume marker.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the installed version.
.SH RESUME
Without opt-out flags, both PR and CI requirements retain their existing defaults.
Recorded opt-outs persist on resume without repeating flags. Legacy markers retain
both requirements. Conflicting flags or invalid policy fields are refused.
These are creation choices, not migration commands: existing live requirements,
custom rules, security settings and history protections must not be weakened.
Python and Rust implement the same policy. With both opt-outs, no empty gate is
created; any remaining gate retains the verified personal owner's exception.
